<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Xiang of Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 637 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duke Xiang of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> ruled the State of Song from 650 to 637 BCE and sought to become hegemon of the Zhou states. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hong">Battle of Hong</a> in 638 BCE he refused to attack the Chu army while it crossed the river or before it formed up, and was defeated and wounded. He is sometimes counted among the Five Hegemons.</p></div>
